  "scope_notes": [
    "SelPt adds selectable point objects and all displayed selectable control/edit grips while retaining existing object picks. It does not expand point-object groups or select previously unselected grip parents.",
    "InvertPt toggles every visible selectable grip by object/index identity and preserves ordinary object selection. Hidden, locked, disabled and stale displays are excluded. Coincident mesh grips remain independent.",
    "Both commands preserve model geometry and both model history stacks. Invalid extra arguments are rejected before changing selection.",
    "The application keeps grip-capable source getters open during both selectors, including affine transforms, SetPt, Smooth and Circle FitPoints. SelPt uses the getter object filter, so Smooth excludes point objects and Circle fitting can include them. Fixed-input and unrelated getters retain their existing command routing.",
    "McNeel quick-reference pages include grips in SelPt while the detailed selection page describes point objects only. The implementation follows the broader quick reference. Fresh native behavior remains unqualified.",
    "Six pending public-command recipes cover ordinary/rational curve and mesh control grips, selected parents and point-object peers. The original 32-case grip transform request remains unchanged. No pending recipe is treated as captured native evidence.",
    "Live Rhino retesting was deferred because of the recorded Wine SSPI startup issue. Solid/SubD grips, per-grip hiding, remaining point-selection commands and performance require further work."
  ],
